{
  "sn12.64:0.1": "Linked Discourses 12.64 ",
  "sn12.64:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "sn12.64:0.3": "If There is Desire ",
  "sn12.64:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn12.64:1.2": "“Mendicants, these four fuels maintain sentient beings that have been born and help those about to be born. ",
  "sn12.64:1.3": "What four? ",
  "sn12.64:1.4": "Edible food, whether solid or subtle; contact is the second, mental intention the third, and consciousness the fourth. ",
  "sn12.64:1.5": "These are the four fuels that maintain sentient beings that have been born and help those about to be born. ",
  "sn12.64:2.1": "If there is desire, relishing, and craving for edible food, consciousness becomes established there and grows. ",
  "sn12.64:2.2": "Where consciousness is established and grows, name and form are conceived. ",
  "sn12.64:2.3": "Where name and form are conceived, there is the growth of choices. ",
  "sn12.64:2.4": "Where choices grow, there is regeneration into a new state of existence in the future. ",
  "sn12.64:2.5": "Where there is regeneration into a new state of existence in the future, there is rebirth, old age, and death in the future. ",
  "sn12.64:2.6": "Where there is rebirth, old age, and death in the future, I say this is full of sorrow, anguish, and distress. ",
  "sn12.64:3.1": "If there is desire, relishing, and craving for contact as fuel … ",
  "sn12.64:3.2": "If there is desire, relishing, and craving for mental intention as fuel … ",
  "sn12.64:3.3": "If there is desire, relishing, and